{"title":"2021 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(De_Moivre&#39;s_Theorem:_Degrees)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (De Moivre's Theorem: Degrees)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(De_Moivre&#39;s_Theorem:_Radians)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (De Moivre's Theorem: Radians)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Binomial_Theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Binomial Theorem)</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3.1_(Real_Parts_Only)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3.1 (Real Parts Only)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_3.2_(Full_Expansions)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3.2 (Full Expansions)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Punxsutawney_Phil\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Hawk_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Hawk Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Using_Polar_Form_and_De_Moivre&#39;s_Theorem)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Using Polar Form and De Moivre's Theorem)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Of the following complex numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, which one has the property that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/7/f779e7d13031a8d827f9338bb8622a9f5e8c4dd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^5$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> has the greatest real part?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/f/42fee78557329c43afe63161c59bc3f90bd474f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }{-}2 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }{-}\\sqrt3+i \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }{-}\\sqrt2+\\sqrt2 i \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }{-}1+\\sqrt3 i\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }2i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"582\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28De_Moivre.27s_Theorem:_Degrees.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(De_Moivre's_Theorem:_Degrees)\">Solution 1 (De Moivre's Theorem: Degrees)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (De Moivre&#39;s Theorem: Degrees)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b7193f66028e13f331d53ff5e6942c4b05587465.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/6/e06020d03e0a4ee334e9037aa3c840c5af4048c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\text{cis}(150)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/169b8d69bd74a91e72ec43123070d770633a340a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/1/d6164d922e40ae65f82cb2cb79c8db117d782273.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\text{cis}(135)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b305929a95b53f14a0ad53eba1d8560626e1f28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/a/1fa867bc73c4fb36e2ff2856dc5f055e2f8d24b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\text{cis}(120)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Taking the real part of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />th power of each we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/2/22267f13830a9237aa78a0f215c3b14b33a74eea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A): }(-2)^5=-32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/4/324b0b4801d4fe6b1d932160ccf4ff93be522a50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B): }32\\cos(750)=32\\cos(30)=16\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"298\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/6/8f63904979c6fca9473c217716499f96114716bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C): }32\\cos(675)=32\\cos(-45)=16\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"310\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/f/8df1318c4fd4946622f44c9f3d19d0d1732d1e9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D): }32\\cos(600)=32\\cos(240)&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"275\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/a/64a775422456d992171681571e08b571ccb2d7cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E): }(2i)^5=32i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"21\" />, whose real part is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/b/09b9084b208f5487c7d83dbf20e32be31ca2e47a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }{-}\\sqrt3+i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"115\" height=\"35\" />.\n</p><p>~JHawk0224\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28De_Moivre.27s_Theorem:_Radians.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(De_Moivre's_Theorem:_Radians)\">Solution 2 (De Moivre's Theorem: Radians)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (De Moivre&#39;s Theorem: Radians)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We rewrite each answer choice to the polar form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859d0b5a2f9d1681c8bd37b037983b88bfbc250f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z=r\\operatorname{cis}\\theta=r(\\cos\\theta+i\\sin\\theta),\\]\" width=\"230\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the magnitude of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/0/3b082fa500291bf2be24d7655214c4802c3e237f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r\\geq0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is the argument of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b448bd981311c4251d88961af1b0a2bb5fd0000.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\leq\\theta&lt;2\\pi.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>By <b>De Moivre's Theorem</b>, the real part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/7/f779e7d13031a8d827f9338bb8622a9f5e8c4dd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^5$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/7/047bb436c7c93eac4c9dbe018ff14309c426a280.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\operatorname{Re}\\left(z^5\\right)=r^5\\cos{(5\\theta)}.\\]\" width=\"163\" height=\"21\" /> We construct a table as follows:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/0/8e0a368fc6fe3887324700fa7d57c2224ee22fc3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{c|ccc|ccc|cclclclcc} &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp;  \\\\ [-2ex] \\textbf{Choice} &amp; &amp; \\boldsymbol{r} &amp; &amp; &amp; \\boldsymbol{\\theta} &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\multicolumn{1}{c}{\\boldsymbol{\\operatorname{Re}\\left(z^5\\right)}} &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\ [0.5ex] \\hline &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp;  \\\\ [-1ex] \\textbf{(A)} &amp; &amp; 2 &amp; &amp; &amp; \\pi &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp;32\\cos{(5\\pi)}&amp;=&amp;32\\cos\\pi&amp;=&amp;32(-1)&amp; &amp; \\\\ [2ex] \\textbf{(B)} &amp; &amp; 2 &amp; &amp; &amp; \\tfrac{5\\pi}{6} &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp;32\\cos{\\tfrac{25\\pi}{6}}&amp;=&amp;32\\cos{\\tfrac{\\pi}{6}}&amp;=&amp;32\\left(\\tfrac{\\sqrt3}{2}\\right)&amp; &amp; \\\\ [2ex] \\textbf{(C)} &amp; &amp; 2 &amp; &amp; &amp; \\tfrac{3\\pi}{4} &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp;32\\cos{\\tfrac{15\\pi}{4}}&amp;=&amp;32\\cos{\\tfrac{7\\pi}{4}}&amp;=&amp;32\\left(\\tfrac{\\sqrt2}{2}\\right)&amp; &amp; \\\\ [2ex] \\textbf{(D)} &amp; &amp; 2 &amp; &amp; &amp; \\tfrac{2\\pi}{3} &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp;32\\cos{\\tfrac{10\\pi}{3}}&amp;=&amp;32\\cos{\\tfrac{4\\pi}{3}}&amp;=&amp;32\\left(-\\tfrac{1}{2}\\right)&amp; &amp; \\\\ [2ex] \\textbf{(E)} &amp; &amp; 2 &amp; &amp; &amp; \\tfrac{\\pi}{2} &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp;32\\cos{\\tfrac{5\\pi}{2}}&amp;=&amp;32\\cos{\\tfrac{\\pi}{2}}&amp;=&amp;32\\left(0\\right)&amp; &amp; \\\\ [1ex] \\end{array}\\]\" width=\"594\" height=\"222\" />\nClearly, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/5/d05433b5d466abe88739e25770126ca4b7a065fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }{-}\\sqrt3+i}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"120\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Binomial_Theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Binomial_Theorem)\">Solution 3 (Binomial Theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Binomial Theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We evaluate the fifth power of each answer choice:\n</p>\n<ul><li>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/3/cb3db983b534373488fba3fdfaf7b692194bb301.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"17\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/3/8a3ac6c43152c6803095ece5fd9241105f9d3633.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-2)^5=-32,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"19\" /> from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/a/b1a671c0ecb7962f18f171f78e36e73af3005b35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{Re}\\left((-2)^5\\right)=-32.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"149\" height=\"23\" /></li></ul>\n<ul><li>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/e/7ae69570c458db7421453f5388296ee0a31fb370.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"17\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/d/3bda10e52372e6a760874d9d1c4412723f86b434.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2i)^5=32i,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"19\" /> from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/b/e0b8d24a97170398cc1246617f6a7029847f0ac0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{Re}\\left((2i)^5\\right)=0.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"118\" height=\"23\" /></li></ul>\n<p>We will apply the Binomial Theorem to each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/7/677ada227f107b748cb1264377fb76f8c91c0843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)},\\textbf{(C)},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/e/4feb78447beef6c93631b0912fb24e7936b6dad3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>More generally, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/e/91ec3f8718b5dad609b860ea272b81ec7c499347.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z=a+bi\\]\" width=\"78\" height=\"14\" /> for some real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/6583a799ce46b06b1cceb493abb45a07c88fd6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b.$\" width=\"11\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p>Two solutions follow from here:\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_3.1_.28Real_Parts_Only.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3.1_(Real_Parts_Only)\">Solution 3.1 (Real Parts Only)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3.1 (Real Parts Only)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>To find the real part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/5/5a5814156e6b848168d390b8b71513b43a880255.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"20\" /> we only need the terms with even powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/693f9874370b7b9fbd513db8f3e9b6c0cb045e6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i:$\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/a/daa74e23d78e689731e917d5f2c5efb9cbd23c0d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\operatorname{Re}\\left(z^5\\right)&amp;=\\operatorname{Re}\\left((a+bi)^5\\right) \\\\ &amp;=\\sum_{k=0}^{2}\\binom{5}{2k}a^{5-2k}(bi)^{2k} \\\\ &amp;=\\binom50 a^{5}(bi)^{0} + \\binom52 a^{3}(bi)^{2} + \\binom54 a^{1}(bi)^{4} \\\\ &amp;=a^5 - 10a^3b^2 + 5ab^4. \\end{align*}\" width=\"395\" height=\"165\" />\nWe find the real parts of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/7/677ada227f107b748cb1264377fb76f8c91c0843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)},\\textbf{(C)},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b305929a95b53f14a0ad53eba1d8560626e1f28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> directly:\n</p>\n<ul><li>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/d/a5d19752c57bc1e73b61c9b9940635a708e80943.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/0/9b078b624dbda08af81996ddfc1256d277370d2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{Re}\\left(\\left(-\\sqrt3+i\\right)^5\\right)=16\\sqrt3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"220\" height=\"45\" /></li></ul>\n<ul><li>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/0/3e0177d15168f7b1af172ddb1ebd4ae8d56b1aea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"17\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/2/0d25107d07a15e67d1089714f1c9903d222d7872.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{Re}\\left(\\left(-\\sqrt2+\\sqrt2 i\\right)^5\\right)=16\\sqrt2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"244\" height=\"45\" /></li></ul>\n<ul><li>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d6d83615701ee2c7146b42a9ddaec6d734aca3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd82222e94c4464874da159f4b71d1e1515c4029.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{Re}\\left(\\left(-1+\\sqrt3 i\\right)^5\\right)=-16.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"219\" height=\"45\" /></li></ul>\n<p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/5/d05433b5d466abe88739e25770126ca4b7a065fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }{-}\\sqrt3+i}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"120\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_3.2_.28Full_Expansions.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3.2_(Full_Expansions)\">Solution 3.2 (Full Expansions)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3.2 (Full Expansions)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The full expansion of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/7/f779e7d13031a8d827f9338bb8622a9f5e8c4dd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^5$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/8/0084c0c472ed0cf901aac2235e01122a84ea0fd6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} z^5&amp;=(a+bi)^5 \\\\ &amp;=\\sum_{k=0}^{5}\\binom5k a^{5-k}(bi)^k \\\\ &amp;=\\binom50 a^{5}(bi)^0+\\binom51 a^{4}(bi)^1+\\binom52 a^{3}(bi)^2+\\binom53 a^{2}(bi)^3+\\binom54 a^{1}(bi)^4+\\binom55 a^{0}(bi)^5 \\\\ &amp;=a^5+5a^4bi-10a^3b^2-10a^2b^3i+5ab^4+b^5i \\\\ &amp;=\\left(a^5-10a^3b^2+5ab^4\\right) + \\left(5a^4b-10a^2b^3+b^5\\right)i. \\end{align*}\" width=\"690\" height=\"197\" />\nWe find the full expansions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/7/677ada227f107b748cb1264377fb76f8c91c0843.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)},\\textbf{(C)},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d6d83615701ee2c7146b42a9ddaec6d734aca3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> then extract their real parts:\n</p>\n<ul><li>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/d/a5d19752c57bc1e73b61c9b9940635a708e80943.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/b/e1bb23cf30d78e6164bca2f8fb48186e99867d8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(-\\sqrt3+i\\right)^5=16\\sqrt3+16i,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"216\" height=\"37\" /> from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/0/9b078b624dbda08af81996ddfc1256d277370d2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{Re}\\left(\\left(-\\sqrt3+i\\right)^5\\right)=16\\sqrt3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"220\" height=\"45\" /></li></ul>\n<ul><li>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/0/3e0177d15168f7b1af172ddb1ebd4ae8d56b1aea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"17\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/f/97f50087ea26fbc236391da05799af3c0513326f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(-\\sqrt2+\\sqrt2 i\\right)^5=16\\sqrt2-16\\sqrt2i,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"264\" height=\"37\" /> from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/2/0d25107d07a15e67d1089714f1c9903d222d7872.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{Re}\\left(\\left(-\\sqrt2+\\sqrt2 i\\right)^5\\right)=16\\sqrt2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"244\" height=\"45\" /></li></ul>\n<ul><li>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d6d83615701ee2c7146b42a9ddaec6d734aca3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/d/5cdaf5d853f061f142e5af5612e21639563f28ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(-1+\\sqrt3i\\right)^5=-16-16\\sqrt3i,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"239\" height=\"37\" /> from which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd82222e94c4464874da159f4b71d1e1515c4029.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{Re}\\left(\\left(-1+\\sqrt3 i\\right)^5\\right)=-16.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"219\" height=\"45\" /></li></ul>\n<p>Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/5/d05433b5d466abe88739e25770126ca4b7a065fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }{-}\\sqrt3+i}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"120\" height=\"35\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Punxsutawney_Phil\">Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Punxsutawney Phil\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtube.com/watch?v=FD9BE7hpRvg\">https://youtube.com/watch?v=FD9BE7hpRvg</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Hawk_Math\">Video Solution by Hawk Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Hawk Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AjQARBvdZ20\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AjQARBvdZ20</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_.28Using_Polar_Form_and_De_Moivre.27s_Theorem.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Using_Polar_Form_and_De_Moivre's_Theorem)\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Using Polar Form and De Moivre's Theorem)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Using Polar Form and De Moivre&#39;s Theorem)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/2qXVQ5vBKWQ\">https://youtu.be/2qXVQ5vBKWQ</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ySWSHyY9TwI?t=568\">https://youtu.be/ySWSHyY9TwI?t=568</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A\">2021 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?t